column120:
15/Oct/13 7:12 PM;557058:443ab871-4096-403e-bd6f-f3534fe417f0;Hi, tuff!

Sorry I didn't get to comment on the pull request in time. To make the added margins
play a bit nicer with IE8 and make the selectors better fit our front end coding standards,
can you tweak the CSS and HTML a bit? If you don't have time, no problem -- I can make
a new issue instead.

The ul on line 4 of _work_header_notes.html.erb should get the class "associations,"
which will also stop the style from affecting any lists the work creator might include
in their notes. The p for the end notes link on lines 60, 62, and 64 of _work_header_notes.html.erb
should get the class "jump." 

And then the CSS on lines 68-70 can change from

.module.notes li:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 1.5em;
}

to

div.preface .associations { 
  margin-bottom: 1.5em;
}

so we're adding the margin to the ul instead of using :last-child. It should also move
up to line 52 of the stylesheet because it's used in the preface (instead of being
a modification unique to the afterword, which is what to mod: afterword section of
the stylesheet is for).

And the CSS on lines 72-74 can change from

.module.notes blockquote + p:last-child {
  margin-top: 1.5em;
}

to 

div.preface .jump {
  margin-top: 1.5em;
}

and also move it out of the mod: afterword section (it could just go right below div.preface
.associations).

